From 48447b72c2b9b1636efa9156cc217cf1e71afced Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 16:09:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Package licenses of vendored lz4 and xxHash sources

The wheel only ships the wrapper's own BSD-3-Clause LICENSE, but the lz4
1.9.4 and xxHash 0.6.5 C sources under lz4libs/ are compiled straight into
the extension modules whenever no system liblz4 is used -- which is how
these wheels are built. Both carry a BSD-2-Clause licence (Yann Collet)
requiring the copyright notice to be reproduced in binary redistributions.

Add the two licence texts beside the vendored sources, declare all three via
license_files so setuptools packages them into dist-info/licenses/, list them
in MANIFEST.in for the sdist, and document the vendored licensing.

Refreshed from upstream PR #344 by pctablet505 to apply on v4.4.5, which
predates the license='BSD-3-Clause' line its setup.py hunk is anchored on.
The xxHash copyright line follows the vendored lz4libs/xxhash.c header
(2012-2016) rather than the wider range used in that PR.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/python-lz4/python-lz4/pull/344]
---
 MANIFEST.in            |  3 +++
 docs/license.rst       |  8 ++++++++
 lz4libs/LICENSE        | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 lz4libs/LICENSE.xxhash | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 setup.py               |  5 +++++
 5 files changed, 66 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 lz4libs/LICENSE
 create mode 100644 lz4libs/LICENSE.xxhash

diff --git a/MANIFEST.in b/MANIFEST.in
index 9561fb1..bfb51c7 100644
--- a/MANIFEST.in
+++ b/MANIFEST.in
@@ -1 +1,4 @@
 include README.rst
+include LICENSE
+include lz4libs/LICENSE
+include lz4libs/LICENSE.xxhash
diff --git a/docs/license.rst b/docs/license.rst
index 3d599fa..5fdc679 100644
--- a/docs/license.rst
+++ b/docs/license.rst
@@ -2,3 +2,11 @@ Licensing
 =========
 Code specific to this project is covered by the `BSD 3-Clause License
 <http://opensource.org/licenses/BSD-3-Clause>`_
+
+This package bundles the LZ4 and xxHash C libraries (under ``lz4libs/``) when
+they are built from source rather than linked against a system-provided
+``liblz4``. Those libraries are covered by their own `BSD 2-Clause License
+<http://opensource.org/licenses/BSD-2-Clause>`_, copyright Yann Collet. The
+license texts are included alongside the vendored sources in
+``lz4libs/LICENSE`` and ``lz4libs/LICENSE.xxhash``, and are packaged with the
+distributed sdist and wheel.
